<title>UK: European cotton slows, no direction from U.S.</title>
<headline>European cotton slows, no direction from U.S.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, ENGLAND 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>European cotton markets failed to shine on Monday as most market operators closed their books ahead of the fast approching Christmas period.</p>
<p>Brokers said many European spinning mills have already shutdown, with trading in raw cotton virtually at a standstill.</p>
<p>The closely eyed New York futures market failed to stimulate interest. &quot;Activity generally remains at a low ebb,&quot; one market source said.</p>
<p>-- LOndon Newsroom +44 171 542 8075</p>
